\section{Materials and Methods}
\subsection{Cohorts, Targets, and Analysis Timing}
PTB-XL folds 1--7 provided 14,955 positive-target training recordings; fold 8 provided 2,129 development recordings. Original component development used seed 42. The public SPH release contains 25,770 recordings from 24,666 patients~\cite{liu2022sph}. The original external population comprised 21,183 recordings from 20,401 patients with at least one mapped target. The five nonexclusive targets were normal ECG (NORM), myocardial infarction (MI), ST--T changes (STTC), conduction disturbance (CD), and hypertrophy or enlargement (HYP), with 13,905, 260, 5,084, 2,465, and 229 positive recordings, respectively.

