\section{Related Work}
\subsection{ECG Representations and Ensembles}
Self-supervised ECG learning includes contrastive representations across space, time, and patients in CLOCS~\cite{clocs2021}, repeated-patient contrastive learning~\cite{pclr2022}, spatiotemporal masked reconstruction in ST-MEM~\cite{stmem2024}, and joint-embedding prediction in ECG-JEPA~\cite{kim2024ecgjepa}. ECG-FM, HuBERT-ECG, and report-aligned multimodal learning extend the range of pretraining strategies~\cite{ecgfm2025,hubert2026,merl2024}. Their published endpoints and adaptation settings differ; the present five-target SPH evaluation does not reproduce those benchmarks.

