Retrospective prevalence adjustment maps the transported raw-score threshold to
\begin{equation}
t'_c=\sigma\{\operatorname{logit}(t_c)-\Delta_c\},\quad
\Delta_c=\operatorname{logit}(\pi_{T,c})-\operatorname{logit}(\pi_{S,c}).
\end{equation}
Source prevalence is fixed at the observed development counts; target prevalence is recomputed in each resample. This research diagnostic requires target labels and a prior-shift assumption~\cite{saerens2002}. The original probabilities and transported vector are unchanged.

